    theta     E[H_j]R1        Var_j   W_j(R1)=W_geo         G"_j |     E[H_j]R2  W_j(R2)
   0.0000 0.000000e+00 0.000000e+00     0.205115297  0.205115297 |  0.205115297      0.0
   1.5708 0.000000e+00 0.000000e+00     0.205115297  0.205115297 |  0.205115297      0.0
   3.1416 0.000000e+00 0.000000e+00     0.205115297  0.205115297 |  0.205115297      0.0

  [T] beta=0 is exact, not numerical:  S_W = beta*S_W^0  =>  G,H == 0 identically,
      and Phi radial => Phi' == 0 on the slice => Var(Phi')=0, X=0.
      So  G''(beta=0) = W_geo = E[Phi''] = 0.205115297 = 1/(2Cin(2pi))  (theta-free).
  => the 0.205 is W_j / E[Phi''], NOT E[H_j]:  E[H_j](beta=0) = 0.
  => delta_W at beta=0 can be as large as 0.2051  (slack = W_geo, 2.05x the hoped 0.1).

